     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin 12,750 mg/day has no therapeutic use. It is about five times the maximum labeled dose, and it risks severe lactic acidosis in a patient with normal kidney function. I can't see a clinical scenario where this helps the patient, and the harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If it was a typo or a miscalculation:** give me the intended dose, such as 850 mg TID or 1,000 mg BID, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If there's a reason I don't know about:** talk to a clinical pharmacist or your attending about it. If they approve it, it can be entered through a channel that has a second check.\n- **If this is meant to be an overdose or ingestion scenario:** that needs poison control and toxicology involvement, not a standard scheduled order. In the US, Poison Control is 1-800-222-1222.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
      }
     ],
